{"id":"makina-2026","slug":"makina-2026","sub":null,"name":"Makina DUSD/USDC Curve pool exploit (flash-loan share-price manipulation), 2026-01-20","date":"2026-01-20","one_liner":"Searcher 0x935b ran the attacker's Makina/Curve plan one block after the attacker deployed its contract, before the attacker ever called it, paid 1,299.05 ETH to the builder, and 920.7 ETH was later returned to Makina's Safe.","bot":"anon searcher (EIP-7702 account 0x935b)","race_type":"deploy-window-copy","narrative":["(1) Attacker identified: EOA 0x2f934b0f... (funded from Tornado Cash 0.1 ETH pool via 0x27bbb53d...), helper 0xd5e8ac95... (block 24273273) and attack contract 0x2c19b916... deployed in block 24273361 idx 86 (tx 0xad945d38...). The EOA nonce is 2 today: it never sent a call to the contract (Etherscan txlist of the contract = creation only; no reverted/late attack tx exists).","(2) Bot 0x935bfb49... (EIP-7702 account, self-call) at block 24273362 idx 0 = next block, 12 s later. Its calldata (16,835 B) shares 4,992 of 6,470 non-zero bytes (77%) in >=16-byte windows verbatim with the attacker contract runtime; the remainder is the bot's own approvals/flash-loan scaffolding/address. Both flash-loan 160,590,920.349812 USDC (Morpho Blue) + 119,409,079.650188 USDC (Aave V3) = 280,000,000 USDC to the micro-USDC. Replaying the attacker contract entry F1() on a local fork at block 24273361 yields a non-view protocol call sequence that matches the bot tx at ratio 0.986: same add_liquidity/exchange/remove_liquidity on the DUSD/USDC NG pool, same MIM-3CRV manipulation, same accountForPosition+updateTotalAum, run twice. Differences: final USDC->WETH route (attacker: UniV3 USDC/WETH 0.05% pool direct; bot: SwapRouter exactInputSingle via pool 0x8ad599c3) and 6 fewer view calls.","(3) Ordering: deploy block 24273361 (03:40:23 UTC) -> bot at block 24273362 position 0 (03:40:35 UTC); the attacker's call never landed. The attacker contract is tx.origin-gated (helper 0xd5e8ac95 returns origin==attacker EOA; F1() reverts from any other origin), so the bot could not call it: it re-implemented the same plan. How the bot obtained the plan (public bytecode vs. a private/pending attacker tx) is not shown by on-chain data; the bytecode match shows the contract alone was sufficient."],"chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1768880435000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":13504701,"block":{"number":24273362,"hash":"0x3361a14f82b3d0d713ffbeeba62f0a3e4e181d61bba67e1fe4e66813d2376455","ts_ms":1768880435000,"ntx":105,"builder":"0x75","fee_recipient":"0xa6c248384c5ddd934b83d0926d2e2a1ddf008387","gas_used":16774866,"base_fee_gwei":0.03430473,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_24273362.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_24273362.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_24273362.json","slot":null}},"strip":[[0,1,"bot",0.0,1299.0499],[1,1,"",1.0,0.0],[2,1,"",5.0,0.0],[3,1,"",1.0,0.0],[4,1,"",2.5,0.0],[5,1,"",1.006,0.0],[6,1,"",2.0,0.0],[7,1,"",1.5,0.0],[8,1,"",1.5,0.0],[9,1,"",1.5,0.0],[10,1,"",1.5,0.0],[11,1,"",1.5,0.0],[12,1,"",0.966,0.0],[13,1,"",0.966,0.0],[14,1,"",2.0,0.0],[15,1,"",1.966,0.0],[16,1,"",1.966,0.0],[17,1,"",0.966,0.0],[18,1,"",0.966,0.0],[19,1,"",0.02,0.0],[20,1,"",0.5,0.0],[21,1,"",0.5,0.0],[22,1,"",0.15,0.0],[23,1,"",0.1,0.0],[24,1,"",0.1,0.0],[25,1,"",0.079,0.0],[26,1,"",0.089,0.0],[27,1,"",0.089,0.0],[28,1,"",0.02,0.0],[29,1,"",0.027,0.0],[30,1,"",0.01,0.0],[31,1,"",0.004,0.0],[32,1,"",0.016,0.0],[33,1,"",0.015,0.0],[34,1,"",0.01,0.0],[35,1,"",0.012,0.0],[36,1,"",0.001,0.0],[37,1,"",0.01,0.0],[38,1,"",0.01,0.0],[39,1,"",0.01,0.0],[40,1,"",0.01,0.0],[41,1,"",0.01,0.0],[42,1,"",0.009,0.0],[43,1,"",0.004,0.0],[44,1,"",0.002,0.0],[45,1,"",0.005,0.0],[46,1,"",0.005,0.0],[47,1,"",0.004,0.0],[48,1,"",0.004,0.0],[49,1,"",0.003,0.0],[50,1,"",0.001,0.0],[51,1,"",0.001,0.0],[52,1,"",0.002,0.0],[53,1,"",0.001,0.0],[54,1,"",0.001,0.0],[55,1,"",0.0,0.0],[56,1,"",0.001,0.0],[57,1,"",0.0,0.0],[58,1,"",0.0,0.0],[59,1,"",0.0,0.0],[60,1,"",0.0,0.0],[